From: Sylvain Zimmer <sylvain@sylvainzimmer.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:56:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] mounts: add sshfs.readonlyNames

A writable project mount lets the guest write .git/hooks or .git/config,
which then run on the host the next time git is used in the project.

sshfs.readonlyNames lists file names that the guest cannot modify, at
any depth of the mount. The builtin SFTP server of sshocker enforces
it on the host, so it holds against a compromised guest.

Validation requires mountType reverse-sshfs, and sftpDriver builtin on
every mount, because the OpenSSH sftp-server serves any host path to
the guest. It also rejects entries that are not plain file names.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
